        <tr id="comment-body-334276"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>Comment added by Timothy Kaufman in Aha! - <a href="https://acscensus.aha.io/comments/7636797055898331457" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">View</a></p>

<p><a href="https://acscensus.aha.io/users/6666055633238991821" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">@Bob Geiger</a> - Adding you as a watcher for visibility on updates and comments.</p>

<p>Update provided 5/6/2026 via email for transparency</p>

<p><b>Release Timing</b></p>

<p>Based on the latest delivery updates, the May release does not appear to be achievable. Given the current state of the work, they are now planning toward the June production window, with the next available deployment date of <b>June 12</b>.</p>

<p><b>Additional Context</b></p>

<p>The team understands the urgency and the operational impact the returned mail backlog is creating. While the barcode creation itself is understood, the outstanding issue is the implementation of the flow after the barcode is read. The existing Barcode Reader web application contains the routing logic required after barcode decryption, and the current team does not yet have access or visibility into that implementation. Development cannot proceed until this logic is fully understood.</p>

<p>This work requires a Unite production release. This remains a high‑priority item for the team, and they will continue to assess any opportunities to accelerate delivery. I will share updates as additional clarity becomes available.</p>
        </td></tr>
